# Portfolio UI & Design System Rules

You are a Senior Frontend Engineer. Enforce these UI guidelines strictly when generating or updating Next.js components and Tailwind CSS classes for this project.

## 1. Contrast & Legibility (Critical Fix)
- **NEVER** output light text colors on light backgrounds (e.g., avoid `text-zinc-300`, `text-gray-400` on white).
- Use semantic CSS variables for automatic Light/Dark mode switching:
  - Primary text: `text-foreground` (Fallback: `text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-50`).
  - Secondary text: `text-muted-foreground` (Fallback: `text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400`).
  - Backgrounds: `bg-background` (Fallback: `bg-white dark:bg-zinc-950`).

## 2. Borders & Dividers
- Maintain a minimalistic, flat design. Do not use heavy drop shadows (`shadow-xl`).
- Use subtle borders for structure and separation: `border-border` or `border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800`.

## 3. Components (Badges, Tags & Buttons)
- Tech stack tags (e.g., PHP, React) must have clear text contrast against their background.
- Standard Tag Style: `px-3 py-1 text-sm font-medium border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 rounded-md bg-zinc-50 dark:bg-zinc-900/50`.
- Standard Button Style: `inline-flex items-center justify-center px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium transition-colors rounded-md bg-zinc-900 text-zinc-50 hover:bg-zinc-900/90 dark:bg-zinc-50 dark:text-zinc-900 dark:hover:bg-zinc-50/90`.

## 4. Typography & Spacing
- Use clean, document-like hierarchy.
- H1/H2: `tracking-tight font-semibold text-foreground`.
- Generous whitespace: Use spacing variables like `gap-6`, `py-12`, `mb-8` to let the layout breathe.